From: Gerard Torres <meganace07@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: don't build vendor GPU/Wi-Fi drivers with -Werror

The PowerVR SGX (pvrsrvkm) and Actions Wi-Fi drivers force -Werror.
Newer GCC adds warnings (stringop-truncation, attributes, ...) on this
old vendor code, which then breaks the build of the GPU module.

